// The provider-AGNOSTIC vocabulary of the AI abstraction: the conversation history shape and a model
// step's outcome. Each provider module maps these to/from its own wire format; the orchestration
// (`ai`) and apps speak only this vocabulary. No provider details leak in here — that is
// the whole point of the abstraction.

@"One turn in a conversation: who spoke (\"user\" / \"model\"), what they said, and any files attached
to it (a Discord attachment, a generated image). Files ride as blob handles; each provider decides
when to inline their content for the model (see the providers' inline policy)."
data turn(role: string, text: string, files: array[file])

@"One tool the model wants to invoke this step — @name@ is its function name (the dispatch key and
the model-facing call/response record), @opaque@ is any provider token that must be replayed
verbatim on the call turn (Gemini's thought signature, OpenAI's call id), @args@ is the model's
argument object as a parsed value (replayed verbatim into the call turn, and dispatched straight
through `reflection.call_agent`, whose delegation boundary revives any `$ref` the model replayed
into the `file` its target expects)."
data tool_call(name: string, opaque: string, args: unknown)

@"A tool's output for the model, keyed by the tool @name@ / @call_id@ so it round-trips as a function
response. @files@ are the `file` values found in the result (a screenshot an MCP tool returned, an
edited image): @text@ already shows their `$ref` handles (the result's wire form), and the provider
additionally inlines their content for the model while the result is fresh."
data tool_result(name: string, call_id: string, text: string, files: array[file])

@"A conversation turn recording the model's tool-call batch — replayed so the next step shows the model what it already asked for."
data call_turn(calls: array[tool_call])

@"A conversation turn carrying the results of a tool-call batch."
data result_turn(results: array[tool_result])

// One conversation-history element. Each provider maps it to its content parts (Gemini text /
// functionCall / functionResponse; OpenAI user|assistant|tool messages), so the function-calling
// loop closes. (Type synonyms take no docs.)
type message = turn | call_turn | result_turn

@"One inference step's decision: a final reply text for the user."
data step_final(text: string)

@"One inference step's decision: invoke a batch of tools (dispatched in parallel, results fed back together)."
data step_call(calls: array[tool_call])

// What a provider returns for one model step.
type step = step_final | step_call
